Given $\tan{A} = \frac{7}{2}$, we have $\dfrac{BC}{AC} = \dfrac{7}{2}$, so:
$$BC = \frac{7}{2} \times AC = \frac{7}{2} \times 12 = 42.$$

Applying the Pythagorean Theorem to triangle $ABC$, we find $AB$:
\begin{align*}
AB &= \sqrt{AC^2 + BC^2} \\
&= \sqrt{12^2 + 42^2} \\
&= \sqrt{144 + 1764} \\
&= \sqrt{1908} \\
&= \boxed{2\sqrt{477}}.
\end{align*}

